# Chat Agent Kernel Deep Dive

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:runic_ai, path: "~/wrk/runic_ai"}
])

Code.require_file("support/runic_ai_livebook.exs", __DIR__)
```

## Purpose

`RunicAI.Recipes.ChatAgentKernel` is the smallest useful conversational agent
in RunicAI. It is the right starting point when you need a normal chat turn
with durable state, but you do not yet need tools, guards, retrieval, or
multi-agent routing.

The general agent shape is:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  user[User input] --> request[TurnRequest]
  request --> prompt[Prompt]
  prompt --> model[LLM call]
  model --> turn[TurnResult]
  turn --> state[Agent.State]
  state --> decision[ContinueDecision]
```

RunicAI makes each box a contract or component you can inspect.

## Provider Setup

```elixir
setup = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.inputs()
```

```elixir
model = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_model!(setup)
llm_opts = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.llm_opts(model, max_output_tokens: RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_max_output_tokens(setup))
```

## Build The Workflow

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Recipes.ChatAgentKernel

workflow =
  ChatAgentKernel.new(
    model: model,
    system: "You are a senior Elixir teacher. Be concise and concrete.",
    llm_opts: llm_opts,
    max_turns: 6
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(workflow)
```

## Run Two Stateful Turns

The first run returns `Agent.State`. The second run passes that state back in,
so the recipe can assemble history and update the conversation.

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.require_openai_key!()

first =
  workflow
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{
    user: "Remember that my demo app is called Lantern."
  })

first_state = ChatAgentKernel.latest_state(first)
ChatAgentKernel.latest_reply_text(first)
```

```elixir
second =
  ChatAgentKernel.new(
    model: model,
    llm_opts: llm_opts,
    system: "You are concise."
  )
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{
    state: first_state,
    user: "What is my demo app called?"
  })

ChatAgentKernel.latest_reply_text(second)
```

```elixir
Kino.Layout.tabs(
  State: Kino.Tree.new(ChatAgentKernel.latest_state(second)),
  Messages: Kino.DataTable.new(Enum.map(ChatAgentKernel.latest_state(second).conversation.messages, &Map.take(&1, [:role, :content]))),
  Productions: Kino.Tree.new(Runic.Workflow.raw_productions(second))
)
```

## Interactive Kernel

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Chat.start(
  ChatAgentKernel,
  [
    model: model,
    system: """
    You are Grug, the friendly caveman. You speak in simple caveman speak with terse simple words easily understood by anyone.

    Despite your simple language you are frighteningly intelligent and philosophical and a master of the socratic method despite using caveman speak.
    """,
    llm_opts: llm_opts,
    max_turns: 8
  ],
  initial_message: "Introduce yourself and remember that I like short answers."
)
```

## When To Move On

Use this kernel until you need one of these:

* tool execution: move to `ConversationalToolAgent`
* approval, waiting, retry, fallback: move to `GuardedOperatorToolAgent`
* summaries, memory, retrieval: move to `SummaryBackedChatAgent`
* workflow-owned state: move to `IntegratedChatAgent`
* child work: move to decomposition recipes
